ility"},"379":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting","content":"Start by locating the failing layer. A Gateway response and an unready pod require different evidence. For rejected issuance or validation results, see PKI troubleshooting; for enrollment, see EST diagnostics."},"380":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting#reproduce-a-single-operation","content":"Note the time in UTC, user or principal, resource, endpoint and result. Avoid repeating a destructive action such as revocation or deletion."},"381":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting#separate-client-gateway-and-service","content":"Check the HTTP status. A 401 points to authentication; a 403, to authorization; a 404, to route or resource; a 5xx, to the service or a dependency."},"382":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting#review-kubernetes-status","content":"Locate unready pods, restarts, recent events and the state of the release."},"383":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/deployment/troubleshooting#query-the-affected-service","content":"Review its /health endpoint and its logs in the same time window. Then follow the indicated dependency: PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, the OIDC provider or the cryptographic engine."},"384":{"