:"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#configure-the-evaluation-dms","content":"Equal duration and window allow immediate renewal testing. These are evaluation values; size production settings according to connectivity and recovery times. Save, reread both authentication blocks and retain the DMS ID. If your console does not expose the independent block, configure and check the resource through the DMS API and DMS guide."},"1454":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#prepare-the-client-and-check-cacerts","content":"Place the four trust and bootstrap files in the new directory. Replace the URL with your installation's URL:"},"1455":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#prepare-the-client-and-check-cacerts","content":"The download must succeed and contain the expected enrollment root. Compare its fingerprint with `device-root.pem`. This check does not turn the response into initial trust or prove that you can issue."},"1456":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#enroll-the-device","content":"Generate a new key and CSR with the selected identifier:"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#enroll-the-device","content":"Request the identity with the bootstrap credential and extract the certificate from the default response:"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#enroll-the-device","content":"If curl fails, use Troubleshooting with the saved body. Do not convert it or repeat the request without querying inventory: a timeout or error can follow persisted issuance."},"1459":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#verify-the-obtained-identity","content":"Expect `device.crt: OK` and exit code 0 from `cmp`. Check the CN, serial, dates, Digital Signature and Client Authentication. The certificate must be a leaf: it must not declare `CA:TRUE` or Certificate Sign use. Check that its validity matches the one-hour profile."},"1460":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#verify-the-obtained-identity","content":"In Lamassu, open `est-device-001`. It must be created with the intended owning DMS, a current identity and the received certificate in its history. Compare the local serial with the slot; thresholds can show a renewal state rather than simply Active."},"1461":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"In a second terminal, enter the same directory and run `umask 077`. Create a local server certificate and start a test consumer. This server trusts `device-root.pem` and requires a valid client identity:"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Leave it running. In the first terminal, connect using the obtained identity:"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Expect HTTP `200`. The client's trust in this local server is its self-signed `consumer.crt`; the server verifies the device against `device-root.pem`. The HTML file displays OpenSSL diagnostic information."},"1464":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"With the same server still running, test that a request without a client certificate is rejected:"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Rejection must correspond to a missing certificate at the server, not a stopped server. Stop the consumer with Ctrl+C after the test. This exercise demonstrates TLS authentication and key possession; your application must also define authorization and revocation consumption. Server options are described in openssl-s\\_server."},"1466":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#result-and-continuity","content":"Check"},"1467":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#result-and-continuity","content":"Expected result"},"1468":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#result-and-continuity","content":"Registration"},"1469":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#result-and-continuity","content":"ID created automatically and correct DMS."},"1470":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#result-and-continuity","content":"Certificate"},"1471":{"id":"/docs/pr-pr