-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","content":"Design root and intermediate authorities and replace certificates or keys without breaking trust."},"1589":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"Design the hierarchy"},"1590":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"Reissuance and rotation are not the same"},"1591":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"When to choose each operation"},"1592":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#key-rotation-procedure","content":"Key rotation procedure"},"1593":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#inventory-the-dependencies","content":"Inventory the dependencies"},"1594":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#create-the-successor-ca","content":"Create the successor CA"},"1595":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#distribute-the-new-trust","content":"Distribute the new trust"},"1596":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#switch-issuance","content":"Switch issuance"},"1597":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#renew-in-batches","content":"Renew in batches"},"1598":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#close-the-overlap","content":"Close the overlap"},"1599":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Cascading revocation"},"1600":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"Checks after the change"},"1601":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","content":"The hierarchy determines the blast radius of any error or compromise. A root signs intermediate CAs; intermediates issue the identities used by devices and services. This separation lets you isolate environments and rotate a branch without replacing all trust."},"1602":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","content":"This procedure is for the PKI operator replacing an authority in use. You need access to CAs, keys and profiles, a dependency inventory and coordination with trust-store and device owners. Before switching issuance, prepare a test cohort and decide the criterion for ending overlap."},"1603":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"For a production installation, use a very restricted root and one or more operational intermediates. Separate intermediates when any of these boundaries change:"},"1604":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"environment, such as production and preproduction;"},"1605":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"owner or operating team;"},"1606":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"device family or manufacturing process;"},"1607":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"region or regulatory requirement;"},"1608":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"cryptographic engine or key policy;"},"1609":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"maintenance window and renewal cadence."},"1610":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"Avoid deep hierarchies without a concrete need. Each level adds chain distribution, validation and one more certificate you must renew."},"1611":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#design-the-hierarchy","content":"A child CA and its end-entity certificates must expire before their issuer. Reserve a margin that allows distributing another chain and renewing dependent certificates."},"1612":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"**Reissuing a CA** creates a new certificate over the existing key. Lamassu generates a CSR with that key, self-signs it if it is a root or asks the parent CA to sign it if it is subordinate. The new certificate becomes active and the CA points to its serial number; the old and new certificates are linked through metadata."},"1613":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"**Rotating a CA** creates a successor key and authority. It is the right choice in the face of compromise, a cryptographic change, an engine migration or non-exportable key policies."},"1614":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#reissuance-and-rotation-are-not-the-same","content":"Lamassu does not allow reissuing an already-revoked CA or a CA whose expiration date has passed. Plan ahead for both conditions."},"1615":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Reissue if the key is still trustworthy and you only need another validity period or an updated certificate."},"1616":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Rotate the key if compromise is suspected, the algorithm changes or you want to move custody to another engine."},"1617":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Create a parallel branch if you cannot update all consumers at the same time."},"1618":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#when-to-choose-each-operation","content":"Revoke immediately only when the risk of keeping the CA outweighs the impact of interrupting the fleet."},"1619":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#inventory-the-dependencies","content":"Locate child CAs, issued certificates, DMSs, connectors and external trust stores. Include devices that may stay offline for weeks or months."},"1620":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#create-the-successor-ca","content":"Generate a new key in the planned engine, create the CA and assign it an explicit profile. Do not reuse the operational identifier to hide that it is a different generation."},"1621":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#distribute-the-new-trust","content":"Add the new root or chain to consumers before issuing with it. If distributing through EST `/cacerts`, explicitly include the required managed CAs and inspect the content; including the issuer does not automatically include every intermediate. Install the new trust in a cohort and verify that it still accepts the previous identity."},"1622":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#switch-issuance","content":"Update the enrollment CA and profile of the DMSs. Keep the additional validation CAs if old certificates still need to be accepted during re-enrollment."},"1623":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#renew-in-batches","content":"Migrate a small cohort, validate mTLS, OCSP and CRL from the consumer and expand progressively. Monitor which devices still present the old chain."},"1624":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#close-the-overlap","content":"Once no legitimate consumer depends on the previous authority, remove it from issuance and from the distributed CAs. Revoke it if policy requires it."},"1625":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Lamassu saves the CA’s revocation, then attempts to revoke child CAs and issued certificates with `CessationOfOperation`. Propagation continues recursively through child CAs. This is not a transaction over the whole hierarchy: some resources may have changed while other updates failed."},"1626":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Resources in `EXPIRED` state and resources already revoked for a final reason reject further status transitions. Per-descendant failures are logged; review the inventory and logs even when the parent operation completes."},"1627":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"`CertificateHold` allows reactivating the parent while it is not expired, but does not restore child CAs or certificates permanently revoked during the cascade. Holding a CA therefore does not provide a reversible pause for its entire branch."},"1628":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#cascading-revocation","content":"Before closing the change, compare the original dependency inventory with final states and verify revocation publication for each issuer. Do not use revocation as the ordinary mechanism to stop issuance: complete migration and remove the CA from operational flows."},"1629":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"The new chain ends in an anchor installed by the consumer."},"1630":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"New certificates contain the expected AKI, SKI, KU, EKU and SAN."},"1631":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"The DMS delivers the correct chain through EST `/cacerts`."},"1632":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"Re-enrollment accepts the old identity during the planned period."},"1633":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"OCSP and CRL respond for the authorities that remain active."},"1634":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"No DMS is left accidentally issuing from the old CA."},"1635":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/ca-hierarchy-and-rotation#checks-after-the-change","content":"See the Trust model to understand the DMS's CA sets and Certificate lifecycle for states and revocation effects."},"1636":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"page","content":"Certification authorities","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Keys, authorities and certificates"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities"},"1637":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","content":"Create, import and operate the authorities that establish your PKI's trust."},"1638":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"Choose a flow"},"1639":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-a-n