-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"Its public certificate in `ca.pem`; this example uses the root created in the previous path."},"2246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"OpenSSL 3.x and a working directory with restricted access."},"2247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"A client identifier: here we use `device-001`."},"2248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"In this flow, the client's key is generated in the browser and must be downloaded when issuance finishes. If you lose it, you must generate a key and issue another certificate. The certificate inventory lets you download the public certificate, but cannot recover this key."},"2249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#start-the-issuance","content":"Open the CA from the previous path, go to **Issued Certificates** and select **Issue New**."},"2250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-20","page_id":"/