s appear in the certificate."},"2259":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"The expected result is `device.crt: OK`. This check uses your explicit root and evaluates the chain, dates and compatibility with the TLS client purpose. Also check for the expected usages and names through the inspection above."},"2260":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"If you use an intermediate CA, the trusted root must be in `ca.pem` and you must supply the intermediates with `-untrusted intermediates.pem`. This variant is covered in the trust model."},"2261":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"The command does not query OCSP or CRL. For revocation checks, continue with Certificate validation. See the openssl-verify reference for its options."},"2262":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#check-that-the-key-matches","content":"In Bash, compare the two public-key digests:"},"2263":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-36/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","